From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] framework: outlined dialogs, menus and toasts; no dimming; white and black

The e-paper interface rules (docs/design/eink-ui.md) for the framework's own
look, which SystemUI, Settings and every app on the default themes use.

Material sets a floating surface apart with a shadow, dims what is behind a
dialog to 40 %, and colours with teal on light grey. On PW3 none of it works:
everything is drawn in software, where no shadow is drawn, so a white dialog
or menu on a white page has no edge; dimming turns the whole page dark grey
and back, two full-panel updates through the slow 16-level waveform; teal
lands on panel level 2, a dark grey hardly different from text; light grey
50 is the panel's white anyway, and the toast's 90 % grey 200 one level below
it, which shows no edge. So:

  * dialogs, popup menus and toasts: white, a black outline of 1dp (2 px) and
    corners of 4dp;
  * backgroundDimAmount 0 in the base, Material and Holo themes: the window
    manager then never shows its dim layer (DimLayer stays hidden at alpha 0);
    an app may still ask for dimming itself;
  * the light theme's background is white and its accent black: a state is
    told apart by shape and fill (checked, on, selected), not by colour.

Only values change; no resource is added, so resource IDs, framework.jar and
the boot image stay as they are, and no app needs compiling again.

--- a/core/res/res/drawable/dialog_background_material.xml
+++ b/core/res/res/drawable/dialog_background_material.xml
@@ -17,7 +17,10 @@
 <inset xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
     android:inset="16dp">
     <shape android:shape="rectangle">
-        <corners android:radius="2dp" />
+        <!-- PW3: an outline instead of the shadow, which software rendering does not draw
+             (docs/design/eink-ui.md: outline black, 1dp = 2 px; corners 4dp). -->
+        <corners android:radius="4dp" />
         <solid android:color="?attr/colorBackground" />
+        <stroke android:width="1dp" android:color="@color/black" />
     </shape>
 </inset>
--- a/core/res/res/drawable/popup_background_material.xml
+++ b/core/res/res/drawable/popup_background_material.xml
@@ -17,9 +17,14 @@
 <shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
        android:shape="rectangle">
 
+    <!-- PW3: an outline instead of the shadow, which software rendering does not draw
+         (docs/design/eink-ui.md: outline black, 1dp = 2 px; corners 4dp). -->
     <corners
-            android:radius="2dp" />
+            android:radius="4dp" />
     <solid
             android:color="?attr/colorBackground" />
+    <stroke
+            android:width="1dp"
+            android:color="@color/black" />
 
 </shape>
--- a/core/res/res/drawable/toast_frame.xml
+++ b/core/res/res/drawable/toast_frame.xml
@@ -17,8 +17,10 @@
 -->
 <shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
        android:shape="rectangle">
-    <!-- background is material_grey_200 with .9 alpha -->
-    <solid android:color="#E6EEEEEE" />
-    <corners android:radius="22dp" />
+    <!-- PW3: white with an outline, as every floating surface (docs/design/eink-ui.md).
+         AOSP's 90 % light grey is one level below the panel's white: no edge. -->
+    <solid android:color="@color/white" />
+    <stroke android:width="1dp" android:color="@color/black" />
+    <corners android:radius="4dp" />
 </shape>
 
